---
title: Roasted habanero salsa
servings: 1
yield: 1 cup
tags: [mexican, vegan, quick]
cuisine: mexican
time: 20 minutes
source: Roasted Habanero Salsa (Taqueria-Style) by Stellanspice, https://stellanspice.com/roasted-habanero-salsa
nutrition:
  calories: 297 kcal
---

Stem the @habanero peppers{5}. Slice the @white onion{1/4}(small) and quarter the @Roma tomato{1}.

> For less heat, take out the seeds and membranes.

Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a #skillet{} over medium-high heat. Blister the habaneros until lightly charred all over.

Add the onion, @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), the tomato and @salt{1%tsp}. Cook ~{2%minutes}, until soft and browned.

Add the @water{1/4%cup}, cover, turn the heat to medium-low and simmer ~{8%minutes}. Uncover for the last ~{2%minutes} and raise the heat to medium to reduce it a little.

Cool slightly, then blend until smooth with a pinch of @salt{}. Streaming in another 1 tbsp oil while blending makes it richer.

Squeeze in a @lime{1%wedge} if you like and adjust the salt. Keeps a week in the fridge.
